# JobBeagle — Enterprise Security Constraints

When changing APIs, auth, payments, or storage, enforce all five:

## 1. Rate limiting & anti-Sybil
- `POST /api/analyze` and `POST /api/extension-capture` must rate-limit by IP and/or user id (in-memory Map or Upstash Redis).
- Preserve device-fingerprint Sybil checks for free Lite credits (`lib/profiles.ts`).

## 2. Payment integrity (Lemon Squeezy)
- Webhook `POST /api/payment/webhook`: verify `x-signature` with HMAC-SHA256 vs `LEMONSQUEEZY_WEBHOOK_SECRET` (`crypto`) **before** mutating credits.
- Idempotency: if `order_id` already processed → return 200, do not grant twice.

## 3. Data privacy / PII
- Resume PDF/DOCX: prefer in-memory parse. Storage uploads need strict RLS (owner-only) + 30-day purge via `/api/cron/purge-reports`.
- Do not put card numbers / extreme secrets into Gemini prompts.
- Account delete (`/api/account/delete`) must hard-delete profile, reports, and stored resume files (CCPA).

## 4. Secrets & architecture
- No service-role / Gemini / LS API keys in Client Components.
- Keep RLS enabled on `profiles`, `analysis_reports`, and related tables.
- Profile credits / `membership_tier`: never client-writable. Lock via migration `011_lock_profile_credit_mutations.sql` (narrow UPDATE grants + entitlement trigger). Mutations only via `service_role` or SECURITY DEFINER RPCs (`decrement_*`, `increment_profile_credits`) and verified Lemon Squeezy webhook.

## 5. Scraping safety
- Extension scrapers: try/catch, delays, graceful degrade to “paste JD manually” — never crash the SW.

Role trigger: user says `@SecOpsExpert` → prioritize this rule.
